WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.477 --> 00:00:16.538
Bobby frowned as he went into the kitchen.

2
00:00:17.839 --> 00:00:19.700
He didn't like cooking class so far.

3
00:00:20.541 --> 00:00:23.062
Chef was strict, and he had so many rules.

4
00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:26.625
But Bobby's eyes lit up when he saw the recipe.

5
00:00:26.645 --> 00:00:29.587
"We're making meatballs!"

6
00:00:29.607 --> 00:00:32.400
"That's right," Chef said.

7
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.622
"Nina and Jason, you can start on the meat mixture.

8
00:00:36.522 --> 00:00:38.843
Bobby and Izzie, you can prep the other ingredients."

9
00:00:40.144 --> 00:00:43.085
"I wanted to do the meat," Bobby mumbled.

10
00:00:45.506 --> 00:00:47.447
Izzie started chopping a garlic clove.

11
00:00:48.528 --> 00:00:49.928
Chef gave Bobby an onion.

12
00:00:49.948 --> 00:00:51.669
"You can chop this."

13
00:00:51.689 --> 00:00:55.591
"That sounds fun," Bobby thought.

14
00:00:56.231 --> 00:00:57.572
He quickly got started.

15
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.382
"Bobby!" Chef frowned.

16
00:01:05.402 --> 00:01:08.344
"There are rules for using knives.

17
00:01:09.284 --> 00:01:11.426
Keep the point of the knife on the cutting board.

18
00:01:12.366 --> 00:01:14.628
Then move the knife up and down—like this.

19
00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:17.650
The onion needs to be finely chopped."

20
00:01:19.411 --> 00:01:20.232
"Yes, Chef."

21
00:01:21.312 --> 00:01:23.734
Bobby didn't know what was wrong with his way.

22
00:01:24.554 --> 00:01:26.596
And the onion was making his eyes water.

23
00:01:27.376 --> 00:01:28.377
He wiped his eyes.

24
00:01:28.397 --> 00:01:32.380
"Now your hands aren't clean, Bobby!"

25
00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:33.493
Izzie said.

26
00:01:33.513 --> 00:01:38.096
"Clean hands are a kitchen rule," Chef said.

27
00:01:38.116 --> 00:01:40.557
"Go wash your hands again."

28
00:01:41.738 --> 00:01:43.619
Bobby sighed as he walked to the sink.

29
00:01:43.639 --> 00:01:45.781
"More rules."

30
00:01:48.443 --> 00:01:50.664
Soon Bobby and Izzie finished chopping.

31
00:01:51.885 --> 00:01:53.706
Chef was standing by the bowl of meat.

32
00:01:53.726 --> 00:01:57.189
"Bring those ingredients over here," he said.

33
00:01:57.209 --> 00:02:02.817
"We already added the egg, bread crumbs, and soy sauce," Jason said.

34
00:02:02.837 --> 00:02:08.821
"Here's the garlic, onion, oregano, and parsley," Izzie said.

35
00:02:10.442 --> 00:02:12.023
She dumped everything into the bowl.

36
00:02:13.404 --> 00:02:15.125
Jason and Nina wet their hands.

37
00:02:16.126 --> 00:02:17.707
Then they mixed everything together.

38
00:02:18.607 --> 00:02:21.529
Chef wet his hands too and grabbed some of the meat mixture.

39
00:02:21.549 --> 00:02:24.031
"Now we'll make the meatballs.

40
00:02:25.192 --> 00:02:27.573
Roll it in your hands until you have a small ball."

41
00:02:29.295 --> 00:02:31.076
Everyone started forming meatballs.

42
00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:33.989
Bobby proudly held up his meatball.

43
00:02:34.849 --> 00:02:37.870
"Look! Mine is almost as big as a baseball!"

44
00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.670
"That's too big!"

45
00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:40.891
Chef snapped.

46
00:02:40.911 --> 00:02:43.311
"It will take too long to cook.

47
00:02:44.271 --> 00:02:46.272
They should be a little smaller than a golf ball."

48
00:02:47.372 --> 00:02:49.573
Bobby sighed and did as he was told.

49
00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:55.355
The kids put their meatballs on an oiled baking sheet.

50
00:02:55.375 --> 00:03:00.296
"We have to wash our hands again," Jason said.

51
00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.441
"We just handled raw meat."

52
00:03:03.621 --> 00:03:05.182
"That's right," Chef said.

53
00:03:07.643 --> 00:03:09.083
He put the meatballs in the oven.

54
00:03:12.705 --> 00:03:15.026
they cook, please pick some green beans in the garden.

55
00:03:15.846 --> 00:03:17.547
Another class will cook them tomorrow."

56
00:03:18.867 --> 00:03:21.088
The kids grabbed baskets and went outside.

57
00:03:21.108 --> 00:03:25.990
"It's nice to be outside," Bobby said.

58
00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:29.332
"Chef has too many rules in the kitchen."

59
00:03:30.428 --> 00:03:32.829
"You like sports," Nina said.

60
00:03:32.849 --> 00:03:35.690
"Sports have lots of rules."

61
00:03:37.051 --> 00:03:37.771
Izzie nodded.

62
00:03:37.791 --> 00:03:40.152
"They make games fair."

63
00:03:40.172 --> 00:03:44.534
"In the kitchen, rules make cooking safe," Jason said.

64
00:03:44.554 --> 00:03:46.034
"I guess."

65
00:03:46.835 --> 00:03:47.735
Bobby shrugged.

66
00:03:48.815 --> 00:03:51.917
When the kids went back inside, the timer was going off.

67
00:03:53.417 --> 00:03:55.378
Chef set the baking sheet on the counter.

68
00:03:55.398 --> 00:03:57.939
"I made a dipping sauce.

69
00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:04.286
It has honey, olive oil, mustard, vinegar, dill, and salt."

70
00:04:04.306 --> 00:04:07.428
"Yum!" Bobby got a meatball and took a bite.

71
00:04:08.208 --> 00:04:09.969
"Ouch! Hot, hot, hot!"

72
00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:10.810
he cried.

73
00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:13.451
"Bobby!" Chef said.

74
00:04:13.471 --> 00:04:16.173
"Never eat anything right out of the oven.

75
00:04:17.353 --> 00:04:18.814
Always let it cool first."

76
00:04:19.675 --> 00:04:21.656
He gave Bobby a cool glass of water.

77
00:04:22.556 --> 00:04:24.637
Bobby swished the water around his mouth.

78
00:04:24.657 --> 00:04:26.978
"I get it now.

79
00:04:27.659 --> 00:04:29.620
Kitchen rules are important!"
